From 610c83fc07bcbf7cf266984f6698e8e00bc3ab88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: donghun <ehdgns1083@pusan.ac.kr>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:32:07 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fpga: add VCU118 (xcvu9p) top-level with BSCANE2 debug
 transport

Port chip_nexus to the AMD VCU118 board. Programs are loaded through the
FPGA's own JTAG port (BSCANE2 USER3/USER4 -> pulp riscv-dbg DTM), so no
extra cable is needed. A small boot ROM prints a banner on the USB-UART
and parks the core until OpenOCD loads a program. DDR4 is not connected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HsWEz2ez3LV2MFsUt4sHDc
